t{d}x}{|7x|\\sqrt{(7x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $7x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=7x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=7\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{7}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}7\\int \\frac{1}{|7x|\\sqrt{(7x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =7\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{7}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(7x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-69475/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d18bdc7-9387-5b2d-98bd-015fa4a1eba7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053/selection/21ad8be0f48dc85b9b01b226cc019dd523b18637790eac04f50ca81eb70126bf" :answer/id #uuid "d8377633-bacf-5c7c-b510-899fe804aff3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(3x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053/selection/1c54bf84a16da56ade56fdfdf6289d536b5bfe18372aebd9803b0feb7328e3be" :answer/id #uuid "41586ce1-c84e-52f5-afa7-4a8d0c32f0e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053/selection/52017bcdd1d694805f9faa7cb1197c3b8a8fc08ff03cc88a801a0454ee6327ba" :answer/id #uuid "74c30c11-17d0-5fed-aef3-6138bd144eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053/selection/59c65d4359bcf4968742f1289c42dd85b8e28822cf75ce0e6ea200a74113128a" :answer/id #uuid "ea14f68c-bd33-5965-bba7-bb3e19cfd9e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053/selection/7086dee718319ab8d51e27b210e4f7ec315ca50e74c648795885a264afe5a6d9" :answer/id #uuid "7dd4ad11-4f50-547b-a2a7-ac496d7c777a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{3}x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc0e267-f80c-5ee2-a278-454fed19ebbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114053/selection/7086dee718319ab8d51e27b210e4f7ec315ca50e74c648795885a264afe5a6d9" :answer-field/choices ["q-114053/selection/21ad8be0f48dc85b9b01b226cc019dd523b18637790eac04f50ca81eb70126bf" "q-114053/selection/1c54bf84a16da56ade56fdfdf6289d536b5bfe18372aebd9803b0feb7328e3be" "q-114053/selection/52017bcdd1d694805f9faa7cb1197c3b8a8fc08ff03cc88a801a0454ee6327ba" "q-114053/selection/59c65d4359bcf4968742f1289c42dd85b8e28822cf75ce0e6ea200a74113128a" "q-114053/selection/7086dee718319ab8d51e27b210e4f7ec315ca50e74c648795885a264afe5a6d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114053" :question/id #uuid "bc2c1d59-0a7c-5002-a982-86e3a36461a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114053" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|x|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{|\\sqrt{3}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{3}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{3}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{|\\sqrt{3}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{3}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d18bdc7-9387-5b2d-98bd-015fa4a1eba7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351827/field-1/15220adc03cfdd78909df30c93eaa6db3dfe4c4cb0891a395cb4f082cc959c85" :answer/id #uuid "78be4c84-ed41-5da4-bd68-0bd038021517" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351827/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "631d3942-73e5-593d-b0d5-41181fe459b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351827/field-1/15220adc03cfdd78909df30c93eaa6db3dfe4c4cb0891a395cb4f082cc959c85" :answer-field/choices ["q-351827/field-1/15220adc03cfdd78909df30c93eaa6db3dfe4c4cb0891a395cb4f082cc959c85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351827" :question/id #uuid "be8bfccc-b567-5c62-9ea9-eace311d32ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-351827" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =15{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{36\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/36)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/36}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{6})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{36-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =5\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351827/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351827"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084/selection/23d59b3888e8828ccbf937282bf5746697f46712f742d4def202638fd7509282" :answer/id #uuid "c8be7c0f-6c6c-5515-aa19-d61eb40f1685" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "a2122e1b-e597-5789-a69c-dbb150b6008f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084/selection/04a379465a1d9a192d346a1ef414650e85cd74eece31c1ce83b8635dce49a739" :answer/id #uuid "44f31708-7364-5b00-bc40-83773c796def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084/selection/6b4ab4c40592f26187c3acfdf186bb8b30345ef09ec3f7a15d2b2ae8b83099b9" :answer/id #uuid "0b740056-8d11-5c1e-837f-82dfab08f2f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084/selection/4cebfca0c261a9499bde84432fdc403251b621653e960f882df963cb649b2b7a" :answer/id #uuid "9320b7ee-1d53-5394-885b-36f361f9eed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd9358d7-9edc-56fd-b26d-a923c3cd4f30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114084/selection/6b4ab4c40592f26187c3acfdf186bb8b30345ef09ec3f7a15d2b2ae8b83099b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-114084/selection/23d59b3888e8828ccbf937282bf5746697f46712f742d4def202638fd7509282" "q-114084/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-114084/selection/04a379465a1d9a192d346a1ef414650e85cd74eece31c1ce83b8635dce49a739" "q-114084/selection/6b4ab4c40592f26187c3acfdf186bb8b30345ef09ec3f7a15d2b2ae8b83099b9" "q-114084/selection/4cebfca0c261a9499bde84432fdc403251b621653e960f882df963cb649b2b7a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114084" :question/id #uuid "5a2898ff-e121-5eb2-975f-1ad5f1f98f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-114084" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114084/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "05f0aba8-7b40-53ac-b543-7d8a81e824ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395/selection/36daa82f4bec5a22e7ba82725971830f1b50dd88483299919d4785b6db46088e" :answer/id #uuid "ec351c8a-a59a-52e6-ab72-a58ed58cdf16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395/selection/ca05dc0d0245a98e052d764ff7ebdac7583d2ee4b3e62c337606f237cbe55b83" :answer/id #uuid "9906929e-8059-5eaf-9d4b-e49539f230a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395/selection/4cebfca0c261a9499bde84432fdc403251b621653e960f882df963cb649b2b7a" :answer/id #uuid "ef52134e-bcee-553e-aa98-461e45e2d4cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395/selection/23d59b3888e8828ccbf937282bf5746697f46712f742d4def202638fd7509282" :answer/id #uuid "8fe2ab70-01b2-54e1-8289-39680848e275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e56ad18-9be3-5335-8236-c82a7b2fc612" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19395/selection/ca05dc0d0245a98e052d764ff7ebdac7583d2ee4b3e62c337606f237cbe55b83" :answer-field/choices ["q-19395/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-19395/selection/36daa82f4bec5a22e7ba82725971830f1b50dd88483299919d4785b6db46088e" "q-19395/selection/ca05dc0d0245a98e052d764ff7ebdac7583d2ee4b3e62c337606f237cbe55b83" "q-19395/selection/4cebfca0c261a9499bde84432fdc403251b621653e960f882df963cb649b2b7a" "q-19395/selection/23d59b3888e8828ccbf937282bf5746697f46712f742d4def202638fd7509282"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19395" :question/id #uuid "af2a59c4-813e-5800-8709-a92b89fd1ce1" :question/math-academy-id "q-19395" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-12{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-12{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3\\cdot (1-4{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(2x)}^{2}.$   \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-0.5$ | $0.5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-12{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.25}^{0.25}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\int }_{-0.5}^{0.5}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-0.5}^{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.5)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-0.5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-19395/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19395"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351291/field-1/3d7e16a5cc571fecd56ab1577bab36394256cea921ff79429323f4faaf6e825d" :answer/id #uuid "d4734356-652b-5a14-8c19-972dd967f7ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287541 :answer-field/choices ["q-351291/field-1/3d7e16a5cc571fecd56ab1577bab36394256cea921ff79429323f4faaf6e825d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351835/field-1/673d869b229f2775502ccf9ffecdbfb5e3720ad9a84c3efc8e96dd3dcc4a640b" :answer/id #uuid "e7e9529f-31a1-5889-89d9-2a0638e13205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351835/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c9e76d-6504-5a1a-a283-636dfd935599" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351835/field-1/673d869b229f2775502ccf9ffecdbfb5e3720ad9a84c3efc8e96dd3dcc4a640b" :answer-field/choices ["q-351835/field-1/673d869b229f2775502ccf9ffecdbfb5e3720ad9a84c3efc8e96dd3dcc4a640b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351835" :question/id #uuid "b13cfa7c-a8cd-51fa-8479-e970b2061f28" :question/math-academy-id "q-351835" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(6x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-36{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(6x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{18}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351835/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
